.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt SEND 2
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm send
.Nd send a scheme-server reply
.Sh SYNOPSIS
See the
.Pa raven-abi
crate (syscall number 0x69).
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
completes a request returned by
.Xr recv 2 .
The reply packet is version 1 and has an appended attachment tail:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
u32 attach_count
struct { u32 handle; u32 rights_mask; } attach[attach_count]
.Ed
.Pp
All fields are little-endian.  At most four attachments are accepted.
Each
.Va handle
is looked up in the replying server's table and must carry
.Dv TRANSFER .
The kernel installs a duplicate in the requesting client's table with rights equal to the server
handle rights intersected with
.Va rights_mask .
A zero mask means all current source rights.
.Pp
The request's captured buffers are kernel-owned copies of the client range (see
.Pa docs/design/capture.md ) .
.Va buffer_addr
and
.Va response_addr
are virtual addresses in the server's address space; reading or writing them touches the
kernel's snapshot, never the client's pages.
A successful read or call response is copied back to the client only if the client's mapping
is still the one captured at request time.
.Pp
For replies other than the
.Dv REPLY_HANDLE
form of
.Xr open 2 ,
the client reply buffer contains the inline data bytes followed immediately by
.Va attach_count
little-endian pairs of the client-table handle and the original rights mask.
The caller must reserve eight bytes per attachment after the data.
For a read reply, the data length is the reply's
.Va buffer_len ;
for Call and Fstat replies it is the inline
.Va data_len .
.Pp
The kernel validates every attachment before taking the client handle-table lock.
If destination insertion or reply-buffer delivery fails, it removes any attachments already
installed for that reply and completes the client with the error.
.Pp
A successful reply may report at most the client's captured input length for
.Dv WRITE
and
.Dv READ ,
and at most the captured response capacity for
.Dv CALL
and
.Dv FSTAT .
A reply that reports more is a protocol violation:
.Nm
returns
.Er EPROTO ,
the client's operation completes with
.Er EPROTO
(never a silent clamp and never a hang), and the server's request handle is closed.
Zero-length and exactly-at-capacity replies are valid.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Rv -std send
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width Er
.It Bq Er EBADF
The request handle is not a request owned by this server.
.It Bq Er EACCES
The handle belongs to another server process.
.It Bq Er EIO
The request was already completed, for example because its client was cancelled.
.It Bq Er EPROTO
The packet, request id, opcode or reported result length is invalid.
.It Bq Er E2BIG
The inline data plus attachments do not fit the captured buffer.
.El
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD ABI v1.
